    {
      "type": "post",
      "id": "7462819434639056896",
      "entityId": "7462819434639056896",
      "linkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/yonathan-levy_linkedin-replaced-its-algorithm-with-a-single-activity-7462819434639056896-NSmK",
      "shareLinkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:share:7462812255982645248",
      "shareUrn": "urn:li:share:7462812255982645248",
      "content": "LinkedIn replaced its algorithm with a single AI system.\nAnd it works differently from what you are used to.\n\nEvery post now goes through four stages before it reaches anyone.\nQuality check, testing, distribution, and matching.\n\n1. The first stage filters out spam and engagement bait instantly.\n2. The second stage shows your post to a small group and watches what happens. If people engage, distribution expands and if they scroll past, it stops.\n3. Who sees it after that depends on how often they interact with you and how closely your topic matches their activity.\n4. The algorithm then matches your post to users based on topic, language, and mentioned companies.\n\nA few numbers worth knowing:\nComments now carry 15x more weight than likes.\nOne save drives 5x more reach than a like and 2x more than a comment.\nPosts with 60+ seconds of dwell time hit 15.6% engagement.\nPosts with under 3 seconds hit 1.2%.\n\nOnce you see how it works, you post differently.",
