    {
      "type": "post",
      "id": "7461007326070800384",
      "entityId": "7461007326070800384",
      "linkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/yonathan-levy_the-best-way-to-sell-on-linkedin-is-to-stop-activity-7461007326070800384-fktl",
      "shareLinkedinUrl": "https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:share:7461007325017894912",
      "shareUrn": "urn:li:share:7461007325017894912",
      "content": "The best way to sell on LinkedIn is to stop selling.\nSounds weird, but the data backs it up.\n\nHubSpot found that inbound leads convert at 14.6%.\nOutbound converts at 1.7%.\n\nThat is not a small gap.\nPeople who find you through your content are 8x more likely to buy than people you cold message.\n\nThe problem is that inbound takes time.\nThree to six months of consistent posting before the pipeline builds.\nThat is why everyone defaults to outbound and skips the content part.\n\nHere is what that looks like:\n\nPhase 1 is research.\nPick your niche, define your ICP, study what is already working in your space.\n\nPhase 2 is building.\nPost 3-4x a week. Track what performs weekly and double down on what works.\n\nPhase 3 is where it pays off.\nBuild a content bank, create a guide that people associate with your name.\n\nYour content does the selling.\nYou just have to give it time.",
